{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777790125,"nonce":"z+Bu5ObGl7lf2gNvK0MB66w5sm0=","title":"Outreach: comp.compression USENET announcement","message":"Post UC2 v3 release announcement to comp.compression USENET. Niche audience but exactly the right one — compression-algorithm specialists, archive-format enthusiasts, dedup researchers.\n\nWhy USENET still works for this audience:\n- comp.compression has low-volume but high-signal traffic; archived in Google Groups and gmane\n- Active maintainers of zstd, brotli, zpaq, etc. read it\n- A serious technical announcement (not just a link drop) often gets thoughtful replies and cross-pollination\n- SDF provides NNTP access from ARPA tier (no MetaARPA needed) — user can post directly via SDF's news server\n\nRequired content (different angle from HN/Lobsters):\n- Lead with the compression engineering: rANS levels 6-9 with content-aware preprocessing (BCJ x86, BWT text, delta filter), CDC + Merkle DAG dedup, SimHash near-dup detection, BLAKE3\n- Benchmark numbers vs comparable archivers (zstd, xz, 7z) on standard corpora (Silesia, enwik9)\n- Backward compatibility as engineering achievement, not just sentiment\n- Open invitation for compression-quality feedback, format-design critique, benchmark methodology review\n\nExpected outcome: 5-15 substantive replies over a few weeks; a couple may be valuable critique that improves the project.\n\nPosting infrastructure:\n- SDF NNTP: news.sdf.org (configure tin/slrn/Pan from SDF shell)\n- Gating: Show HN/Lobsters writeup (separate issue) should land first — earns external reference for the USENET post to point to","files":null}]}